(18171, 5799, 3, 492, '2024-02-14 08:33:57', 'Upon asking queries with the end-user of the situation that happened, there was unwanted printing from other units. This occured due to wrong IP addressing of the installed printer of the other units. Instructed the other units to stop printing from this printer and uninstalled this printer from their laptop and desktops. ', NULL, 'Active', 'Assured client that there was only a mistake in the IP addressing of the printers.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(18172, 5811, 3, 492, '2024-02-14 08:37:35', 'End-user stated that the printer was previously installed from the Wi-Fi network of DOH EV CHD. Upon checking, the printer was disconnected from the network. Connected printer to the Wi-Fi network - CHD_Employee and provided static IP address of - 192.168.3.49 with hostname (08PT-HPU-07). Connected two units to be able to print to the printer.', NULL, 'Active', 'Canon G4010 series printer driver was installed to the laptop and desktop.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(18173, 5815, 3, 492, '2024-02-14 08:40:22', 'Client had the hard time of opening the MS Powerpoint file located in the desktop of his unit. It turns out that the file was just loading due to multiple opened applications and an outdated hardware system of the unit.', NULL, 'Active', 'Reset default application when opening .pptx files to MS Office Powerpoint.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(18174, 5817, 3, 492, '2024-02-14 08:45:32', 'Epson L5290 - newly delivered and supplied to the requesting office. Proceeded to refill ink to the ink tank and performed ink charge after. Provided static IP address - 192.168.3.23 with hostname (PRN08-BUDGET-09). Added hostname to the hostname monitoring from NAS. Then, connected three (3) computers from the requesting office with printer driver of Epson L5290 compatible with Windows 10 and Windows 7.', NULL, 'Active', 'Renamed the printer to EPSON L5290-BUDGET', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
