(21778, 6983, 3, 492, '2024-08-27 05:56:21', 'Upon inspection, desktop unit was functional and in good condition. But when rebooting the desktop unit, the error prompts that there is no HDD installed for boot. But when pressing the keys, CTRL+ALT+DELETE, the desktop unit will reboot with no error. Transferred the SATA cable from port1 to port3 but the problem just escalated. Same in altering the bootup type from UEFI to legacy. Restored the BIOS to its default settings and set the priority bootup to EFI then the HDD. In conclusion, the HDD is defective, require more inspection.', NULL, 'Active', 'Instructed the client to reboot the desktop unit by pressing the keys, CTRL+ALT+DELETE once the error prompts.', 57, 825, NULL, 'N/A', 'N/A'),
(21779, 6990, 3, 492, '2024-08-27 05:57:44', 'Upon inspection, desktop unit was functional and in good condition. But when rebooting the desktop unit, the error prompts that there is no HDD installed for boot. But when pressing the keys, CTRL+ALT+DELETE, the desktop unit will reboot with no error. Transferred the SATA cable from port1 to port3 but the problem just escalated. Same in altering the bootup type from UEFI to legacy. Restored the BIOS to its default settings and set the priority bootup to EFI then the HDD. In conclusion, the HDD is defective, require more inspection.', NULL, 'Active', 'Duplicate request with ticket number: 240822085125', 57, 825, NULL, 'N/A', 'N/A'),
