(1422, 28, 29, 0, '09052205811', '', 'The reason I have asked assistance from the ICTU is that when I saw what was written in the RIS, it was confusing and not specific.  I returned the RIS to the MMS and the MMS staff said that it is in the system.  ICTU takes charge of our office systems.  Correct me if I am wrong.  I have conducted a research and the following are what I found:\r\n\r\nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN OFFICE SUPPLIES AND SPARE PARTS:\r\n\r\n*  WHAT ARE OFFICE SUPPLIES?\r\n\r\n    Office supplies are consumables regularly used in office and businesses and other organizations, by individuals engaged in written communications, records-keeping or \r\n    bookkeeping, janitorial and cleaning, and for storage of supplies or data.\r\n\r\n* WHAT ARE SPARE PARTS?\r\n\r\n   Spare parts are duplicate parts which are used to replace lost or damaged parts of machines or equipment.\r\n\r\nOur Brother MFC-L5900DW  at the General Services Section uses this specific copier ink TN-3448.\r\n\r\nThe item requested by our section was the DRUM UNIT  with specification DR - 3445 which is one of the spare parts of our BROTHER MFC-L5900DW and said item is not consumable in nature and every time it is replaced,  it needs a WASTE MATERIAL REPORT, \r\nhence, this request to correct the system.\r\n\r\nIf I accept or sign the RIS, it might mean that I received both office supplies and spare parts when in fact it is only the spare part that we have requested.  The following are\r\nthe entries in the RIS:\r\n\r\nPc.          INK (GENERAL SERVICES)\r\n              BROTHER MFC-L5900DW (DRUM UNIT DR-3455) (DOH-EV-CHD8)\r\n\r\nWill be grateful if you will help enlighten all concerned about this matter.\r\n\r\nThank you.', '2021-03-10 03:32:11', 'Active', 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL),
(1423, 347, 351, 0, '09262214119', 'ncdudoh@gmail.com', '', '2021-03-10 08:26:55', 'Active', 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL),
